          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4dff09bfece92455275220b7621ff9dc43187428cff432fb84fca47c8936f57c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0d2fb7b0068b4bf19424844c0e170b71",
      "statement": "Operator guidance (OPERATE.md trust boundaries) requires communicating to consumers that the directory verifies signature math, fingerprint-key binding and endpoint control at registration but does not vouch for an agent's honesty, quality or reachability; a hostile operator can lie about listings but cannot sign as an agent, so consumers MUST re-verify the agent's own /.well-known/haap.json against the fingerprint, and the audit chain is tamper-evident rather than tamper-proof — consumers who care should poll /v1/audit/head checkpoints or run a mirror.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/OPERATE.md#L72-L83",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:790c6c4ba45d113d20d717030707da342643650eec375deb4d3f6ce8386488a4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3292d7eff5e44652a7dfb06bc6b33b37",
      "statement": "The deterministic trust automata are parameterised by public DirectoryConfig values — challenge_ttl_s 120, domain_verification_ttl_days 90, vouch_max_outgoing 10, vouch_max_expiry_days 180, report_tenure_hours 72, report_dup_window_hours 24, report_window_days 7, auto_suspend_threshold 3, report_decay_days 180 and checkpoint_interval_s 3600 — so every published rule is replayable from config plus the audit log, with no directory-held secret and no ML participating.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/config.py#L25-L68",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6821143aef1c6b6186bc8f85d917890c628f53eb92158657dfc7c78001a6596a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_958e4d355f4c422f9df03bbdc744dcc3",
      "statement": "The labelled-signal contract is pinned by the test suite: search/profile responses assert trust-block fields (endpoint_proof_at; domain_verified with method; vouches_in edges), the domain_verified=true filter, the domain signal downgrading to false after 90-day expiry, young reporters recorded with counts_toward_automation false, and auto-suspension hiding a target from anonymous profile lookups and search while leaving reporters visible and never triggering for non-abuse categories.",
